course: dictionary
lesson: 4293
title: Greyhound: fast as a dog, fast as a whale
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A greyhound is a tall, thin dog with long legs. It can run very fast, so people race greyhounds and some hunt with them. Many are kind, gentle pets too. «Ex-racing greyhounds often have never lived in a house and need time to learn that a home is safe.» So a racing greyhound may need patience before it feels calm in a home.
explain: Writers sometimes compare an animal to a greyhound to show speed. «Fin whales race like greyhounds.» You do not need to know much about whales to get the idea: the word greyhound tells you the whales are very fast.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The fin whale is so fast it is called the greyhound of the sea.» This is a nickname. It is a way of saying the whale is as quick as the famous racing dog. Nicknames like this help you picture how something moves, even if you have never seen it.
fact: A greyhound is a tall, thin dog with long legs.
fact: Greyhounds are very fast runners, and they are used for racing and hunting.
fact: Many retired racing greyhounds become calm pets.
fact: «Greyhounds can reach about seventy kilometres an hour thanks to long legs.»
fact: Greyhound is also the name of a well-known long-distance bus company in the US.
exercise: «Fin whales race like greyhounds.» What does this suggest about fin whales? | They are very small | They are very quiet | They are very slow | *They are very fast
exercise: What is a greyhound? | A small, fluffy dog with short legs | *A tall, thin dog with long legs that runs very fast | A large bus that carries people far away | A bird that cannot fly
exercise: «Greyhounds can reach about seventy kilometres an hour thanks to long legs, a deep chest with big lungs and a bendy spine.» Which feature helps a greyhound run fast? | Loud bark | Thick fur | *Long legs | Short tail
test: «Yet at home they sleep most of the day.» What does this tell you about greyhounds at home? | *Calm and relaxed | Hungry all the time | Always running around | Always barking
test: «The fin whale is called the greyhound of the sea.» What does this nickname tell you? | It has fur | *It is very fast | It lives on land | It is a kind of bird
exam: What does the word greyhound mean? | A large sea animal with a spout | *A tall, thin, very fast dog with long legs | A kind of bird that cannot fly | A bus that goes to the seaside
